    <statement><p>Find a vector <m>\mathbf{a}</m> that has the same direction as <m>\langle -6, 9, 6 \rangle</m> but has length <m>4</m>.</p>
<p>Answer: <m>\mathbf{a} =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left&lt;-1.94028,2.91043,1.94028\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p>The given vector has length <m>\left| \langle -6, 9, 6 \rangle \right|
= \sqrt{(-6)^2+9^2+6^2}= \sqrt{153}</m>, so a unit vector in the direction of 
<m>\langle -6, 9, 6 \rangle</m> is 
<m>\mathbf u = \frac{1}{\sqrt{153}}\langle -6, 9, 6 \rangle</m>.</p>
<p>A vector in the same direction but with length  <m>4</m>  is</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle 4 \mathbf u = \frac{4}{\sqrt{153}} \langle -6, 9, 6 \rangle 
=  \left \langle \frac{-24}{\sqrt{153}} , \frac{36}{\sqrt{153}},
\frac{24}{\sqrt{153}} \right \rangle</m>.</p>
</solution>
